{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#448","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#448","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#448\",\"parent_revision\":\"0f2d150dcace73d5c469b122043f536209570029dd9e8c26d09165f1c27d3e15\",\"root_revision\":\"0f2d150dcace73d5c469b122043f536209570029dd9e8c26d09165f1c27d3e15\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\ntask_status_hook.py writes LastActivity timestamps on every Write/Edit/Bash call during task execution, but nothing reads those timestamps to detect or act on stalled agents.\\n\\nA stalled agent (one that starts but produces no tool activity for N minutes) currently holds its task IN PROGRESS indefinitely, blocking dependent tasks and consuming a concurrency slot.\\n\\n**Proposed behaviour:**\\n- Add a stall-checker script (or extend implementation_manager.py) that queries all IN PROGRESS tasks, computes `now - LastActivity`, and flags any task exceeding a configurable threshold (default: 10 min).\\n- Flagged tasks: update status to BLOCKED with a note `stall detected after Nm of no activity`; delete the active-task context file.\\n- Hook integration: run the stall checker as a SubagentStop or periodic check within implement-feature before dispatching the next wave of ready tasks.\\n- Configurable via task file metadata or CLAUDE.md: `stall_timeout_minutes`.\\n\\n**Acceptance criteria:**\\n- IN PROGRESS task with LastActivity older than threshold is detected and marked BLOCKED automatically.\\n- implement-feature does not re-dispatch a stalled task without explicit operator action (rerun or manual status reset).\\n- Stall events are logged with task ID, last activity time, and elapsed minutes.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | `task_status_hook.py` writes `LastActivity` timestamps | AVAILABLE | Item description confirms this |\\n| 2 | `implementation_manager.py` has status query and update capability | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py` |\\n| 3 | `implement-feature` wave dispatch loop location | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/` |\\n| 4 | Active-task context file format and location | DERIVABLE | Check implementation_manager.py for context file handling |\\n| 5 | `stall_timeout_minutes` config field format for task files | MISSING | Convention not yet established |\\n\\nVerdict: READY with one minor convention to establish (config field format).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP1 Feature. Affects implement-feature orchestration and implementation_manager.py. Medium complexity. Risk: false-positive stall detection on legitimately slow tasks; mitigated by configurable threshold.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- A stall-checker script or extension to `implementation_manager.py` queries all IN PROGRESS tasks, computes `now - LastActivity`, and flags tasks exceeding the configurable threshold (default: 10 min)\\n- Flagged tasks: status set to BLOCKED with note `stall detected after Nm of no activity`; active-task context file deleted\\n- `implement-feature` runs the stall checker before dispatching the next wave of ready tasks\\n- Stall timeout configurable via task file metadata or CLAUDE.md: `stall_timeout_minutes`\\n- Stall events logged with task ID, last activity time, and elapsed minutes\\n- `implement-feature` does not re-dispatch a stalled task without explicit operator action (rerun or manual status reset)\\n- Regression: tasks that complete normally in under threshold time are not flagged\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/implementation_manager.py` \u2014 add stall detection query and BLOCKED transition\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/` \u2014 add stall check before wave dispatch\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 document `stall_timeout_minutes` field\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/task_format.py` \u2014 add optional `stall_timeout_minutes` field\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an implement-feature orchestrator, I need automatic stall detection for in-progress tasks so that agents that start but produce no activity for N minutes are flagged BLOCKED and their concurrency slot is released, preventing indefinite pipeline blockage.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **stall detection for subagent tasks** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: OpenAI Symphony SPEC.md \u00a78.4 \u2014 stall_timeout_ms fires after 5 min of no Codex events, terminates worker, schedules retry\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a74630ba95ca39fab1e2c109e76bc19733c8c1857d2c71cc8b3e42ea843af95a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTCGZQ\"}"}